  "body": "Was stacked on #512 (pocket and slot recognition), which merged on 2026-11-10; this PR now holds only its own two commits against main.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe Model page gains a **Pockets and slots** section (#511):\n- **Detect pockets / slots** runs `app::recognize::pockets_of` once per click.\n- Each recognised feature is a row: kind, slot width/length/ends, floor Z, depth, tightest corner, islands.\n- Each row has a **Create Pocket / Create Slot** button. It queues one `CreateOperation`, selects the new op and opens its page, as one undo step. The button's tooltip names the tool it will use (the last document tool that fits the kind, the ribbon's quick-add rule). With no tool it is disabled.\n- The scan is view state keyed by model and document version. Any document change hides the list, and Create refuses (\"detect pockets again\"), so no row offers coordinates the part no longer has.\n\nThe planning (name, seed, tool-sized helix, feature mapping) moved into `app::recognize::plan_operation`, with the shared seed in `operation::seed_params`. The MCP `detect_pockets {create}` tool calls the same code, so a click and an agent create the same operation. `ui` holds no recognition logic (layering ui → app).\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `pockets_tests` (ui lib), 4/4:\n  - `detect_lists_the_slot_and_the_pocket`: a part with a through slot and a closed pocket lists both, with the right row text.\n  - `create_adds_each_operation_as_one_undo_step`: the slot becomes a Slot cutting into the stock and the pocket a Pocket on the part's floor face, each opens its page, and one Undo removes each.\n  - `a_changed_document_makes_the_list_stale`\n  - `a_model_without_geometry_is_refused_by_name`\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick`, escalated to batch, 812 s: geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion and app all green. This includes `mcp`, `mcp_pockets`, `pocket_recognition`, `operations` and `project_roundtrip`, so the moved seed is behaviour-identical.\n- ui: only the five known reds that are also red on main: three headless tests that need a GPU adapter, and `structural::shell_structure_dark/light` (`v0.0.0`).\n- clippy `-D warnings` on app and ui is clean after the follow-up commit.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Clicking the section in a running GUI. The ui state tests drive the same methods the page calls.\n- Hover-highlighting each floor in the viewport. It is left out (see the decision record) and can be a follow-up if wanted.\n\nChangelog: The Model page detects a model's pockets and slots and creates the Pocket or Slot operation for each with one click (#511)\n\nFixes #511\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
